cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PALMS: Provenance-Aware Linking of Multimodal Spatial-omics"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Srinivasa Rao"
    family-names: "Rao"
    email: "srinivasa.rao@nds.ox.ac.uk"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rao-genomics-lab/palms"
url: "https://palms.readthedocs.io"
abstract: >-
  PALMS is a napari-based viewer for Xenium 3.x spatial transcriptomics output that brings
  transcripts, cells, histology and genomic overlays into one coordinate space, and records
  every action the user takes as a node in a provenance graph. The graph is exported as a
  Jupyter notebook that replays the session from the raw data, so an exploratory analysis
  ends with runnable, reviewable code rather than an undocumented result. It runs on Linux,
  macOS and WSL2.
keywords:
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - spatial omics
  - provenance
  - reproducibility
  - multimodal imaging
  - image registration
  - napari
  - single-cell
  - Xenium
license: MIT
version: 1.0.1
date-released: "2026-09-01"

